# Overview

<p class="lede">
<code>ppd</code> is a CLI, a set of vitest helpers and a Claude Code skill for people who write
<a href="https://github.com/getpaseo/paseo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Paseo</a> plugins. It gives you a dev daemon
you can break, checks your plugin against what the host really accepts, and drives the web UI and a phone, without
ever touching the Paseo you use every day.
</p>

<Callout kind="info" title="Unofficial">

A community project, not affiliated with or endorsed by the Paseo team. It relies on parts of Paseo that are not a
public API and was verified on Paseo {meta.verifiedPaseo}. See [Compatibility](/docs/compatibility).

</Callout>

<h2 id="why">Why it exists</h2>

It was built while shipping a real plugin (a PDF and Office viewer). Each of these cost days, and each is now a
check, a guard or one command:

- **Hand-built isolated daemons.** Testing a plugin means a temp home, a free port, plugins and the web UI on, relay
  off. One wrong flag and you restart or reconfigure your real daemon on port 6767. `ppd daemon up` does it safely in
  one line.
- **Host-contract surprises found late.** An icon name the app's Lucide build lacks makes the button silently vanish.
  `class` syntax in a dependency passes on web and crashes on phones (Hermes). A module the host does not provide
  throws only at load. `ppd check` finds these before install.
- **No agent to test against.** Hooks, timeline cards and injected MCP tools need agent turns. The fake agent runs
  scripted turns with no credentials.
- **Registry submission gotchas.** Issues filed with `gh issue create` miss the `submission` label and are ignored.
  Git listings never get automatic update PRs. The validator fails on macOS temp paths. `ppd registry` handles all
  three.
- **Device testing friction.** `adb reverse`, which device, is the phone unlocked, and never pressing keys on someone
  else's phone. `ppd android up` connects it and reports state, read-only.

<h2 id="what-you-get">What you get</h2>

| Piece | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `ppd` CLI | `create`, `daemon`, `install`, `dev`, `paseo`, `web`, `android`, `doctor`, `check`, `registry`, `release`. See [Commands](/docs/commands). |
| `paseo-plugin-devkit/vitest` | `describeHostContract(dir)`: one vitest test per host-contract check. |
| `paseo-plugin-devkit/testing` | `runChecks`, `assertWithinRpcBudget` and the pieces behind `ppd check`. |
| `paseo-plugin-devkit` | Daemon, install and fake agent helpers for tests: `runFakeAgentTurn`, `sendFakeAgentTurn`, `agentTimeline`, `pluginRows`. |
| `paseo-plugin-devkit/web` | `PaseoWeb`, the Playwright page object behind `ppd web`. |
| Claude Code skill | `skills/paseo-plugin-dev`: the isolated-daemon loop, the safety rules, the host-contract table and device testing, for an agent working on your plugin. |

<h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>

| For | You need |
| --- | --- |
| Everything | Node {meta.node}, macOS or Linux. |
| `daemon`, `install`, `dev`, `web`, fake agent | The Paseo CLI. The desktop app ships it; `ppd` also finds it inside `/Applications/Paseo.app`. |
| `check` with the real compiler | The Paseo desktop app, or a [getpaseo/paseo](https://github.com/getpaseo/paseo) checkout in `PASEO_SOURCE`. Without either, `check` runs a labeled approximation. |
| `web` | Google Chrome, or a Playwright Chromium matching `playwright-core`. |
| Hermes checks | `react-native` as a devDependency of the plugin (it ships `hermesc` and the Hermes VM), or `HERMESC` and `HERMES`. |
| `android` | `adb` (Android platform-tools) and the Paseo app on the phone. |

`ppd doctor` reports all of these in one go.

<h2 id="install">Install</h2>

In a plugin:

```sh
npm install -D paseo-plugin-devkit
npx ppd doctor
```

Outside a project, name the package: the npm name `ppd` belongs to an unrelated package.

```sh
npx --package paseo-plugin-devkit ppd create ~/code/my-plugin
```

